{{!
    @template theme_dimensions/category_course_modal

    The course dialogue's frame: core/modal with three blocks overridden. The dialogue carries the
    plugin's own class, which qualifies every rule of its stylesheet. The header keeps core's close
    button and a visually hidden title: the course's visible title is on the cover inside the body,
    so it scrolls away with the picture it is printed on, and the header is laid over the cover's
    corner. The hidden title labels core's root until categorycoursemodal moves that id to the
    cover's title and removes it, so the dialogue has one heading, the visible one. It keeps
    data-region="title" because core/modal's constructor reports an exception when the header has
    none. The body and the footer stay core's blocks, which the module fills with the two parts of
    category_card_modal.

    Everything else core/modal brings is kept: the focus trap, Escape, the close button, the
    backdrop and the focus given back to the control that opened it.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "title": "Pre-hospital Care",
        "body": "<div class=\"dim-cmodal__sheet\"><h2 class=\"dim-cmodal__title\" data-region=\"title\">Pre-hospital Care</h2></div>",
        "footer": "<div class=\"dim-cmodal__actions\"><a class=\"btn dim-cmodal__button dim-cmodal__button--primary\" href=\"https://example.com/course/view.php?id=42\">Continue course</a></div>"
    }
}}
{{< core/modal }}
    {{$classes}}dim-cmodal__dialog{{/classes}}
    {{$headerclasses}}dim-cmodal__close{{/headerclasses}}
    {{$header}}
        <h2 id="{{uniqid}}-modal-title" class="visually-hidden" data-region="title">{{title}}</h2>
    {{/header}}
{{/ core/modal }}
